 r←Test_Server_209(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;html
⍝ Every release of a major version line has a "details" and a "dependencies" page of its own,
⍝ and to a search engine those look like near-duplicates of one another. Neither is therefore
⍝ offered for indexing.
⍝ What is checked here is the absence of a canonical link naming the "versions" page. That is
⍝ how this was solved first, and it does not work: a search engine honours a canonical link
⍝ only within a set of pages it considers duplicates of one another, and the "versions" page
⍝ is not in that set. It must not come back.
⍝ That the pages carry "noindex" cannot be checked here: the INI file of the test server sets
⍝ CONFIG:NoIndexing, so every page it serves carries the tag whatever the code does.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages/details/aplteam-APLProcess-0.2.0'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'aplteam-APLProcess-0.2.0'⍷html
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'<link rel="canonical"'⍷html

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages/dependencies/aplteam-APLProcess-0.2.0'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'aplteam-APLProcess-0.2.0'⍷html
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'<link rel="canonical"'⍷html

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
